"Variable \"{variable}\" ({label}) has {n} levels: {levels}. Only "
"\"{positive}\" is treated as positive; every other level ({others}) is "
"counted as NEGATIVE. If any of those levels represent equivocal or "
"indeterminate results, this recoding can bias sensitivity, specificity, "
"predictive values, and likelihood ratios and make them difficult to "
"interpret. Recode the variable to two levels and set equivocal results to "
"missing if that is not what you intend."
